  "details": "<p>Coordinates were determined by eye using Google Earth on 27 October 2011. Imagery date was 8/27/2009 (Image copyright 2011 GeoEye). Eye alt: 210m.</p>\r\n<p>The peripteral Doric temple of Apollo at Corinth dates ca. 540 B.C. and replaced an earlier temple of ca. 625 B.C. The temple\u2019s ground plan of 6 x 15 columns grant it the elongated proportion of Archaic Doric temples.</p>\r\n<p>\u00a0</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The second temple of Apollo at Corinth whose reconstructed remains are visible on the site today. The structure dates ca. 540 B.C.",
